    "bio": "A Representative from New Jersey; born in Jersey City, Hudson County, N.J., August 20, 1924; graduated from Lincoln High School, 1942; commissioned a naval officer at Columbia University, 1944; served in the United States Navy aboard the U.S.S. <i>Mount McKinley, </i>1944-1946; B.A., Dartmouth College, Hanover, N.H., 1947; J.D., New York University School of Law, 1950; LL.M., New York University School of Law, 1955; graduate work, Hague Academy of International Law, The Hague, Netherlands; admitted to the New Jersey bar in 1951 and commenced practice in Jersey City; served in the New Jersey State senate, 1965-1972; elected as a Democrat to the Ninety-sixth and to the six succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1979-January 3, 1993); was not a candidate for renomination in 1992 to the One Hundred Third Congress; is a resident of New York, N.Y.",
